*   Harmonic Palette: A tuning system pitched strictly to A=432Hz. It relies on 1950s Latin-big-band minor-ninth chords dissolved into infinite microtonal acid swells and Pythagorean drone intervals.
*   Production Signatures: 
    1. Rallentando-Phasing: Brass stabs passed through vintage 1950s magnetic tape units that intentionally flutter as train speeds change.
